# 📝 Private Notes – Weather Monitoring Station

## 📌 Project Summary

The Weather Monitoring Station is a simple Arduino project that measures temperature and humidity using a DHT11 sensor. The values are shown on a 16×2 I2C LCD display. I built this project to understand how sensors work with Arduino and how to display real-time data.

---

# 💡 Project Idea

The idea of this project was to make a small weather monitoring system that can continuously show the current temperature and humidity of the surrounding environment. It is simple, easy to build, and suitable for beginners.

---

# 🛠 Development Notes

- Collected all the required components before starting.
- Connected the DHT11 sensor and I2C LCD with the Arduino Uno.
- Checked all the wiring before powering the circuit.
- Installed the required Arduino libraries.
- Wrote and uploaded the Arduino program.
- Tested the sensor readings several times.
- Arranged the jumper wires neatly after testing.
- Prepared all project documents after completing the hardware.

---

# ⚠ Problems Faced

- At first, one jumper wire was loose.
- I selected the wrong COM port while uploading the code.
- I checked the DHT11 pin connection again because the sensor was not responding.
- The LCD brightness needed slight adjustment to make the text easy to read.

---

# 🔧 How I Solved Them

- Reconnected the loose jumper wire.
- Selected the correct COM port in the Arduino IDE.
- Verified all pin connections using the circuit diagram.
- Adjusted the LCD contrast properly.

